DTEND:20171024T162500Z
SUMMARY:#t3e: Outreach+
DESCRIPTION:Presentations  Engaging Communities\, Unlocking Archives\, and Advancing Research through CrowdsourcingBenjamin Wiggins\, Kevin Erhman-SolbergUniversity of Minnesota\, United States of America Want to engage broad communities\, transcribe archival manuscripts\, or generate a massive original data set? In this presentation\, we'll teach you how to harness the wisdom of the crowd for community engagement and scaleable research support with Zooniverse--the world&rsquo;s largest platform for people-powered research.   Imperfect attendance: Using data to plan digital scholarship outreach at Indiana UniversityNicholas Homenda\, Erika JennsIndiana University Libraries\, United States of America Workshops and presentations offered by the Indiana University Libraries enhance digital scholarship outreach to broad audiences. This paper will build upon analyses of digital scholarship activities at IU and beyond\, investigating attendance patterns\, attendees&rsquo; disciplinary profiles\, and promotional effectiveness in order to inform programming development for upcoming semesters.   Exploring our special collections: Outreach workshops to promote community engagement and digital literacyJenn Riley\, Sarah Severson\, Deena Yanofsky\, Nathalie Cooke\, Jennifer GarlandMcGill University\, Canada The McGill University Library and Archives has piloted workshops for local secondary school students using digitized special collections and HistoryPin maps. This presentation will describe the workshop design\, lessons learned\, and next steps at McGill to build a systematic community outreach program focusing on crowdsourcing and digital literacy.
