DTSTART:20171024T203000Z
DTEND:20171024T212500Z
SUMMARY:#t7b: Surveying the landscape of data governance and ethics
DESCRIPTION:Surveying the landscape of data governance and ethicsJacob Levernier(1)\, John Borghi(2)\, Jacqueline Quinless(3)\, M. Scott Thompson(4)1: University of Pennsylvania\, United States of America; 2: California Digital Library\, United States of America; 3: University of Victoria\, Canada; 4: CLIR Postdoctoral Fellow\, United States of America The purpose of this panel is to describe the current data governance landscape\, identify tools useful for shaping features of that landscape\, and consider how individuals in these areas may collaborate with each other and others\, including in industry\, as data sharing and re-use become more systematized\, commonplace\, and incentivized. 
CATEGORIES:DLF SESSIONS
LOCATION:Butler\, Pittsburgh\, PA\, United States
SEQUENCE:0
UID:0d92024484720e7fde8c87b97cf65e67
URL:http://dlfforum2017.sched.com/event/0d92024484720e7fde8c87b97cf65e67
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20171024T203000Z
DTEND:20171024T212500Z
SUMMARY:#t7c: Service Management - Sharing Experiences and Defining a Community of Practice
DESCRIPTION:Service Management - Sharing Experiences and Defining a Community of PracticeCatherine Aster(1)\, Wendy Gogel(2)\, Nick Homenda(3)\, Sarah Severson(4)\, Helenmary Sheridan(5)\, Gail Steinhart(6)\, Vanessa Venti(2)1: Stanford Libraries; 2: Harvard University; 3: Indiana University Libraries; 4: McGill University Library; 5: University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign; 6: Cornell University Library This panel will explore the developing community of practice for service management in the digital library\, archive and museum settings. Alongside a proposed definition of service management\, panelists will describe their roles at their respective institutions. Audience queries will drive the most substantial part of the hour with facilitated dialogue.
CATEGORIES:DLF SESSIONS
LOCATION:Cambria\, Pittsburgh\, PA\, United States
